Original commit body from 987b7df56f0dce536d57fac3946ecc6b9751ea70:

tree-sitter-odin nests the call_expression of ``fmt.println(..)`` inside
the member_expression, and both handlers fired: the member branch emitted
the ``fmt.println`` edge and the call branch a second, bare ``println``
one. The call branch now stands down when its parent is a
member_expression; the member branch is the one that knows the module.

Red on dev: ['odin:external:0-0:fmt.println:unresolved',
'odin:external:0-0:println:unresolved'] for one call. Green: the first
only. The bare unresolved path (a plain call to an unknown procedure),
which the spurious edge had been covering, gets its own test.

